# W17 — "after selecting something with world breaker the arrow seems to be
# originating from the very top right of the screen ... i would expect it to
# show from the played card on the stack." Seat 0 (human) holds World Breaker
# ("When you cast this spell, exile target artifact, enchantment, or land")
# and enough mana (6 generic + 1 green = 7) to cast it. EIGHT legal targets
# exist (seat 0's own seven lands plus seat 1's one Island) so Forge opens a
# real InputSelectTargets ask rather than auto-targeting the only choice —
# the same auto-target shortcut `auto-target.state`'s own header explains.
# World Breaker itself is still on the stack (not yet on any battlefield) the
# moment that ask opens, which is exactly the case `cardBox` cannot find a
# board element for.
